{"id":"gr20-corsica","title":"GR20, Corsica","who":"Classic route · \"Europe's toughest trek\"","when":"June to September, when the refuges are staffed","vehicle":"On foot, 12–16 days, refuges (no wild camping)","kind":"walk","color":"#9a3412","summary":"About 180 km and 12,000 m of climbing along Corsica's granite spine from Calenzana to Conca: scrambles with chains, high ridges above the sea, mountain lakes and shepherds' huts selling cheese. The steep, alpine north ends at Vizzavona, with a train out; the gentler south runs through beech forests.","sources":[{"label":"Bookatrekking: GR20 stages, difficulty and refuges","url":"https://bookatrekking.com/en/blog/gr20-corsica/"},{"label":"Much Better Adventures: GR20 guide in 15 stages","url":"https://muchbetteradventures.com/magazine/gr20-corsica-guide-15-stages"}],"approximate":"Main refuges; the line follows mountain paths where they were found.","km":167,"bbox":[8.8527,41.7299,9.3358,42.5084],"stops":[{"name":"Calenzana","place":"Calenzana, Corsica","at":[42.5084,8.8553],"text":"A long, hot first climb from the village.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Calenzana-warly.jpg/500px-Calenzana-warly.jpg","page":"Calenzana","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Calenzana-warly.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Ortu di u Piobbu","place":"Refuge d'Ortu di u Piobbu","at":[42.465,8.9059],"text":"The first refuge, about 1,570 m.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Verda48a.jpg/500px-Verda48a.jpg","page":"Monte Cinto","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Verda48a.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Carozzu","place":"Refuge de Carozzu","at":[42.4263,8.9005],"text":"Over the ridge and down past the Spasimata slabs and footbridge.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Gr20.jpg/500px-Gr20.jpg","page":"GR 20","source":"ht